# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# Only system-level settings live here. The four behavior levers (three node prompts
# plus the tool description) live in the database as versioned rows -- never here,
# never hardcoded. That is what makes rollout and rollback possible.
#
# Temperature and the loop cap are neither: they are constants in the code
# (agent/llm.py and agent/graph/runner.py). Not environment variables on purpose --
# a knob that quietly differs between two machines makes their evaluation results
# incomparable. See TO-06.

# Two deployment-only variables, neither needed locally:
#
#   PORT       Which port to bind. Defaults to 8000. Render injects its own and
#              fails the deploy if nothing is listening there (TO-33).
#   SEED_DEMO  Any non-empty value loads datasets/demo_seed.json at startup. Set on
#              Render, where the filesystem is wiped on every spin-down and there is
#              no shell to re-seed from; left unset locally, because canned rows
#              mixed into a database you are poking at obscure what you just did.
#              Run `python scripts/seed_demo.py load` by hand instead (TO-32).

# --- pick ONE provider, set MODEL to match, fill in that provider's key ---
#
# Gemini is what this was built and measured on. The other two are here because
# the take-home provisions Anthropic and OpenAI keys but not a Google AI Studio
# one, and a reviewer should not have to go get a key to run this (TO-31).
#
#   MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite     GEMINI_API_KEY      verified end to end
#   MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5       ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   wired, not verified
#   MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini               OPENAI_API_KEY      wired, not verified
#
# "Wired, not verified" is meant literally: the key check, the price table and the
# provider routing are all in place, but I had no Anthropic or OpenAI key to run
# against. The specific thing that could break is structured output -- the design
# assumes a real responseSchema, and a provider that only emulates it in the prompt
# would reintroduce the parse failures that assumption removed. If a run dies in
# plan or reflect with a validation error, that is what happened; switch back to
# Gemini. See TO-31.
#
# The version is pinned on purpose. The "-latest" aliases drift when the provider
# repoints them, and a silent model change shows up as "my prompt edit caused a
# behavior change", which is the single hardest kind of regression to diagnose.
#
# Run `uv run python -m ask_luma.cli models` to see what your key can reach.
MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite

GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Path to the SQLite file. Mounted as a volume in docker-compose.
# DB_PATH=./data/app.db
